<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/binomial-model> {
  ex:l5-sequence-formula cd:body "Probability of one specified sequence: 0.2 squared multiplied by 0.8 to the eighth power."@en .
  ex:l5-binomial-formula cd:body "Binomial count probability: the number of arrangements multiplied by the probability of one arrangement."@en .
  ex:l5-binomial-moments-formula cd:body "Expected count n times p; variance n times p times one minus p."@en .
  ex:l5-zero-formula cd:body "Probability of zero positives: one minus p, raised to the number of independent trials n."@en .
  ex:binomial-distribution a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Binomial distribution"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:l5-binomial-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-binomial-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The binomial model describes the count of successes in a fixed number of independent binary trials with a common success probability. The probability of one specified sequence is the product of its trial probabilities. The probability of a count includes every arrangement with that count. The expected count is the number of trials multiplied by the success probability; the variance additionally contains the failure probability. Neither expectation nor one observed count fixes the result of another series."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l5-source-r-binomial ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-sequence-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "One specified order only"@en ; cd:latex "P(\\text{this sequence})=(0.2)^2(0.8)^8" ; dct:hasPart ex:l5-sequence-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:l5-ms-seq-event, ex:l5-ms-seq-probs, ex:l5-ms-seq-product ; cd:hasSource ex:l5-source-r-binomial ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-sequence-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l5-sequence-legend-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-sequence-legend-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and conventions"@en ; dct:references ex:l5-ms-seq-event, ex:l5-ms-seq-probs, ex:l5-ms-seq-product ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-seq-event a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "P(this sequence)" ; cd:mathNotation "P(\\text{this sequence})" ; cd:body "P gives the probability of this exact order of ten outcomes. The equals sign states its value; probability is dimensionless."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-seq-probs a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "0.2, 0.8" ; cd:mathNotation "0.2,\\ 0.8" ; cd:body "Per-trial probabilities of a positive and a negative result, respectively. They sum to one."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-seq-product a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "powers and product" ; cd:mathNotation "(0.2)^2(0.8)^8" ; cd:body "Powers repeat factors: two positives and eight negatives. Parentheses group each base; adjacent factors multiply under independence."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-binomial-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "All arrangements with the chosen count"@en ; cd:latex "P(K=k)=\\binom{n}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-k}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l5-binomial-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:l5-ms-bin-event, ex:l5-ms-bin-params, ex:l5-ms-bin-choose, ex:l5-ms-bin-product ; cd:hasSource ex:l5-source-r-binomial ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-binomial-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l5-binomial-legend-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-binomial-legend-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and conventions"@en ; dct:references ex:l5-ms-bin-event, ex:l5-ms-bin-params, ex:l5-ms-bin-choose, ex:l5-ms-bin-product ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-bin-event a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "P(K=k)" ; cd:mathNotation "P(K=k)" ; cd:body "Probability of exactly k positives. K is the random count; k is a chosen integer from 0 to n. Equality inside the brackets defines the event."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-bin-params a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "n, p" ; cd:mathNotation "n,\\ p" ; cd:body "n is the fixed trial count. p is the common positive-result probability; 1-p is the negative-result probability."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-bin-choose a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "binomial coefficient" ; cd:mathNotation "\\binom{n}{k}" ; cd:body "Number of ways to place k positives among n trials. This symbol counts arrangements; it is not division."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-bin-product a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "powers and multiplication" ; cd:mathNotation "p^k(1-p)^{n-k}" ; cd:body "Powers repeat factors; n-k counts negatives. Adjacent factors multiply under independence. The outer equality gives probability; all terms are dimensionless."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-binomial-moments-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Centre and spread across repeated series"@en ; cd:latex "E[K]=np,\\qquad \\operatorname{Var}(K)=np(1-p)" ; dct:hasPart ex:l5-moments-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:l5-ms-mom-counts, ex:l5-ms-mom-probs, ex:l5-ms-mom-operators, ex:l5-ms-mom-product ; cd:hasSource ex:l5-source-r-binomial ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-moments-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l5-moments-legend-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-moments-legend-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and conventions"@en ; dct:references ex:l5-ms-mom-counts, ex:l5-ms-mom-probs, ex:l5-ms-mom-operators, ex:l5-ms-mom-product ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-mom-counts a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "K, n" ; cd:mathNotation "K,\\ n" ; cd:body "K is the random number of positives in a series; n is the fixed number of independent trials."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-mom-probs a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "p, 1-p" ; cd:mathNotation "p,\\ 1-p" ; cd:body "Common positive- and negative-result probabilities. Subtraction takes the complement to one; probabilities are dimensionless."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-mom-operators a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "E, Var" ; cd:mathNotation "E[\\cdot],\\ \\operatorname{Var}(\\cdot)" ; cd:body "Expectation and variance across repeated series; brackets contain their argument. Mean uses counts, variance squared counts."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-mom-product a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "products and equality" ; cd:mathNotation "np,\\ np(1-p)" ; cd:body "Adjacent factors multiply; parentheses group 1-p. Equalities give the model mean and variance, not guaranteed outcomes."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-zero-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "A prediction under an assumed probability"@en ; cd:latex "P(K=0)=(1-p)^n" ; dct:hasPart ex:l5-zero-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:l5-ms-zero-event, ex:l5-ms-zero-complement, ex:l5-ms-zero-power ; cd:hasSource ex:l5-source-r-binomial ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-zero-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l5-zero-legend-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-zero-legend-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols and conventions"@en ; dct:references ex:l5-ms-zero-event, ex:l5-ms-zero-complement, ex:l5-ms-zero-power ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-zero-event a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "P(K=0)" ; cd:mathNotation "P(K=0)" ; cd:body "Probability of no positives. K is the random positive count; equality inside the brackets specifies zero. The result is dimensionless."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-zero-complement a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "p, 1-p" ; cd:mathNotation "p,\\ 1-p" ; cd:body "p is an assumed per-trial positive probability; 1-p is the negative probability. This is prediction, not estimation from data."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-ms-zero-power a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "n and power" ; cd:mathNotation "(1-p)^n" ; cd:body "n is the fixed independent trial count. The power multiplies n negative-result probabilities; parentheses group the base. The outer equality states this probability."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/specifications/level5-binomial-workshop> {
  ex:unit-level5-probability-models cd:hasFocusConcept ex:binomial-distribution .
  ex:l5-b03a-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Build the sampling model: one sequence"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "The survey count includes all arrangements"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Explain variation between sample surveys"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Zero findings do not establish absence"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b06-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Ten samples are not ten repeats"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b06-media a cd:MediaAsset ; cd:uri "/chemometrics/level5-samples-vs-repeats.svg"^^xsd:anyURI ; cd:mediaType "image/svg+xml" ; cd:alternativeText "Two schematic panels. Left: ten numbered sampling positions spread across a water body, each supplying a separate water sample. Right: one collected water sample supplies ten laboratory measurements. Environmental samples can inform population findings under a justified design; laboratory repeats describe analytical repeatability for that sample. The drawing does not establish representativeness or independence."@en ; cd:body "Separate water samples can inform the water body, if the selection design justifies it. Repeating one sample describes laboratory repeatability, not environmental coverage."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-b03a-model a cd:BinaryExperiment ; cd:binaryExperimentMode "sequence" ; cd:binaryTrialCount 10 ; cd:binaryTargetCount 2 ; cd:binaryPositiveProbability 0.2 ; cd:binarySeed 20261030 ; cd:binaryPositiveLabel "positive"@en ; cd:binaryNegativeLabel "negative"@en ; cd:binaryUnitLabel "Sample"@en ; cd:binaryTrialName "Bernoulli trial"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-model a cd:BinaryExperiment ; cd:binaryExperimentMode "arrangements" ; cd:binaryTrialCount 10 ; cd:binaryTargetCount 2 ; cd:binaryPositiveProbability 0.2 ; cd:binarySeed 20261030 ; cd:binaryPositiveLabel "positive"@en ; cd:binaryNegativeLabel "negative"@en ; cd:binaryUnitLabel "Sample"@en ; cd:binaryTrialName "Bernoulli trial"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-model a cd:BinaryExperiment ; cd:binaryExperimentMode "distribution" ; cd:binaryTrialCount 10 ; cd:binaryTargetCount 2 ; cd:binaryPositiveProbability 0.2 ; cd:binarySeed 20261030 ; cd:binaryPositiveLabel "positive"@en ; cd:binaryNegativeLabel "negative"@en ; cd:binaryUnitLabel "Sample"@en ; cd:binaryTrialName "Bernoulli trial"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-model a cd:BinaryExperiment ; cd:binaryExperimentMode "zero" ; cd:binaryTrialCount 10 ; cd:binaryTargetCount 0 ; cd:binaryPositiveProbability 0.2 ; cd:binarySeed 20261030 ; cd:binaryPositiveLabel "positive"@en ; cd:binaryNegativeLabel "negative"@en ; cd:binaryUnitLabel "Sample"@en ; cd:binaryTrialName "Bernoulli trial"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b06-model a cd:BinaryExperiment ; cd:binaryExperimentMode "assumptions" ; cd:binaryTrialCount 10 ; cd:binaryPositiveProbability 0.2 ; cd:binarySeed 20261030 ; cd:binaryPositiveLabel "positive"@en ; cd:binaryNegativeLabel "negative"@en ; cd:binaryUnitLabel "Sample"@en ; cd:binaryTrialName "Bernoulli trial"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-b03a-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "Probability of one specified order"@en ; cd:body "Assume independent results with 20% positive probability. This particular order has two positives and eight negatives."@en ; cd:hasBinaryExperiment ex:l5-b03a-model ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:l5-b03a-input, ex:l5-b03a-product ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:l5-b03a-edge ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03a-input a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "One specified sequence"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03a-product a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Multiply independent trial probabilities"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03a-edge a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-b03a-input ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-b03a-product ; skos:prefLabel "each specified outcome contributes one factor"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "From one arrangement to a count"@en ; cd:body "Keep ten independent trials and a 20% positive probability. We now accept any order with exactly two positives."@en ; cd:hasBinaryExperiment ex:l5-b03b-model ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:l5-b03b-input, ex:l5-b03b-count ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:l5-b03b-edge ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-input a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Different positive positions"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-count a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Same total positive count"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-edge a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-b03b-input ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-b03b-count ; skos:prefLabel "include every arrangement, not only the first"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "Exact binomial model probabilities"@en ; cd:body "Independent trials with a common positive probability. These bars are model probabilities, not simulated frequencies."@en ; cd:hasBinaryExperiment ex:l5-b04-model ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:l5-b04-input, ex:l5-b04-output ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:l5-b04-edge ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-input a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Trial count and common positive probability"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-output a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Probabilities, expected count and variance"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-edge a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-b04-input ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-b04-output ; skos:prefLabel "parameters determine the model, not a guaranteed series"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "Zero observed does not mean impossible"@en ; cd:body "Ten negative results leave population finding frequency uncertain. The calculation assumes 20%; it does not estimate the probability that absence is true."@en ; cd:hasBinaryExperiment ex:l5-b05-model ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:l5-b05-input, ex:l5-b05-output ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:l5-b05-edge ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-input a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Known probability: predict a count"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-output a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Observed count: estimate an unknown probability"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-edge a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-b05-input ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-b05-output ; skos:prefLabel "change the statistical question, not the meaning of probability"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-b06-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "Check the trial unit and model conditions"@en ; cd:body "Fixed trial count, binary outcomes, a common probability and independence must describe the actual sampling process."@en ; cd:hasBinaryExperiment ex:l5-b06-model ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:l5-cond-n, ex:l5-cond-two, ex:l5-cond-p, ex:l5-cond-i, ex:l5-case-a, ex:l5-case-b, ex:l5-case-c ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:l5-cond-edge1, ex:l5-cond-edge2, ex:l5-cond-edge3, ex:l5-cond-edge4, ex:l5-cond-edge5, ex:l5-cond-edge6 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-n a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; cd:visualRole "condition" ; skos:prefLabel "Fixed trial count"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-two a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; cd:visualRole "condition" ; skos:prefLabel "Two defined outcomes"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-p a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 3 ; cd:visualRole "condition" ; skos:prefLabel "Common probability"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-i a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 4 ; cd:visualRole "condition" ; skos:prefLabel "Independent outcomes"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-case-a a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 5 ; cd:visualRole "case" ; skos:prefLabel "A: Ten independently selected water samples from one defined population."@en ; cd:body "Potentially binomial: one binary decision per sample, common conditions and probability. Check the actual sampling design; independence is an assumption."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-case-b a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 6 ; cd:visualRole "case" ; skos:prefLabel "B: Ten repeat measurements of the same water sample."@en ; cd:body "Not ten independent environmental samples. Technical decisions could be binomial conditional on this sample under stable conditions and independent measurement errors."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-case-c a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 7 ; cd:visualRole "case" ; skos:prefLabel "C: Samples from two sites with different positive-result probabilities."@en ; cd:body "Not a simple binomial sum with one common probability. Independent Bernoulli trials with unequal probabilities give a Poisson-binomial count, not a Poisson count."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-edge1 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-cond-n ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-case-a ; skos:prefLabel "check"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-edge2 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 2 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-cond-two ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-case-a ; skos:prefLabel "check"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-edge3 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 3 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-cond-p ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-case-a ; skos:prefLabel "check"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-edge4 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 4 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-cond-i ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-case-a ; skos:prefLabel "check"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-edge5 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 5 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-cond-i ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-case-b ; skos:prefLabel "check the independent unit"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-cond-edge6 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 6 ; cd:sourceNode ex:l5-cond-p ; cd:targetNode ex:l5-case-c ; skos:prefLabel "check the common probability"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/paths/level5-binomial-opening> {
  ex:path-level5-binomial-opening cd:forTopic ex:binomial-distribution ; cd:hasStep ex:l5-b03a-step, ex:l5-b03b-step, ex:l5-b04-step, ex:l5-b05-step, ex:l5-b06-step .
  ex:l5-b03a-step a cd:PathStep ; cd:position 3 ; cd:usesScene ex:l5-b03a-scene ; cd:usesResource ex:l5-b03a-title, ex:l5-b03a-flow, ex:l5-sequence-formula ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-step a cd:PathStep ; cd:position 4 ; cd:usesScene ex:l5-b03b-scene ; cd:usesResource ex:l5-b03b-title, ex:l5-b03b-flow, ex:l5-binomial-formula ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-step a cd:PathStep ; cd:position 5 ; cd:usesScene ex:l5-b04-scene ; cd:usesResource ex:l5-b04-title, ex:l5-b04-flow, ex:l5-binomial-moments-formula ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-step a cd:PathStep ; cd:position 6 ; cd:usesScene ex:l5-b05-scene ; cd:usesResource ex:l5-b05-title, ex:l5-b05-flow, ex:l5-zero-formula ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b06-step a cd:PathStep ; cd:position 7 ; cd:usesScene ex:l5-b06-scene ; cd:usesResource ex:l5-b06-title, ex:l5-b06-media ; cd:authoredResource true .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/level5-binomial-workshop> {
  ex:l5-b03a-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:binomial-distribution ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-b03a-heading, ex:l5-b03a-visual, ex:l5-b03a-math ; cd:narration "B03a. Explain the complete calculation directly. The illustrated order contains two positives and eight negatives. Each positive contributes 0.2 and each negative 0.8; independence permits multiplication. Powers count repeated factors. The resulting probability is 0.0067108864, about 0.6711%. This concerns one specified order, not every possible arrangement with two positives. The formula, its complete legend and the factors are visible together from the start. This is an illustrative sequence, not a fresh random simulation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03b-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:binomial-distribution ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-b03b-heading, ex:l5-b03b-visual, ex:l5-b03b-math ; cd:narration "B03b. All 45 arrangements and the binomial formula are shown immediately. Each row is a possible order; the plus signs mark its two positive positions. With independent trials and a common probability, every one of these arrangements has the same probability as the previous slide. Adding them gives 0.301989888, about 30.20%. The binomial coefficient counts arrangements. It is not an arbitrary correction or a division sign. The model counts positives wherever they occur. This explanation does not require a sequence of separate position changes or audience prompts."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b04-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:binomial-distribution ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-b04-heading, ex:l5-b04-visual, ex:l5-b04-math ; cd:narration "B04. Three complete model views replace the earlier prediction steps. The formula and legend remain visible throughout. First, ten trials at probability 0.2 give expectation 2 and variance 1.6. Second, ten trials at 0.5 give a symmetric distribution, expectation 5 and variance 2.5. Third, one hundred trials at 0.2 give expectation 20 and variance 16. The horizontal count range changes with the trial count. Absolute count variance grows with n, whereas relative-frequency variance decreases. These are exact model probabilities, not simulated frequencies or a continuous density. The vertical scale stays fixed at zero to 100%. Expectation is an average across repeated series, not a guaranteed result. The remote changes between the three substantive comparisons; there are no prediction questions or sliders."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b05-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:binomial-distribution ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-b05-heading, ex:l5-b05-visual, ex:l5-b05-math ; cd:narration "B05. The complete zero-count calculation is visible immediately. Under a known hypothetical 20% per-trial positive-result probability, zero positives among ten independent trials has probability 0.1073741824, about 10.74%. This is prediction under a stated assumption, not the probability that the assumption is true. Estimation instead starts from an observed count and an unknown event probability. A zero observed fraction does not prove zero probability. Ten negative screening results do not establish absence of PFAS, and technical repetitions do not become independent environmental samples. Confidence-bound calculations remain optional later material."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b06-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:binomial-distribution ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l5-b06-heading, ex:l5-b06-visual ; cd:narration "Compare the two pictures. On the left, ten separate water samples are taken from selected water units. Each sample supplies one binary screening decision. With a justified selection design, these findings can inform the positive-finding frequency in the defined water population. The positions are schematic, not a proposed monitoring plan; spreading dots across a map does not prove representativeness or independence. On the right, one collected water sample is measured ten times in the laboratory. Those results characterize analytical repeatability for that sample, not coverage of ten environmental units. Repeats also do not establish analytical accuracy or absence of bias. The technical decisions could themselves have a binomial count conditional on this sample, if measurement errors are independent and the positive-result probability remains constant. Their environmental sample size is still one. For a simple binomial model, check a fixed trial count, two defined outcomes, a common probability and independence. Independent Bernoulli trials with unequal probabilities give a Poisson-binomial count, not a simple binomial or automatically a Poisson count. A large biased sample is not repaired by its size. The key distinction is the unit selected, not merely the number of results. Next change from binary decisions per selected sample to particle events within a fixed water volume."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:l5-b03a-heading a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-b03a-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03a-visual a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-b03a-flow ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DiagramRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l5-b03a-math a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l5-sequence-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
